## 4. host_run call path

  Shared read-only: `cli/host_run.oo` (207 lines), `cli/find_compiler.oo`.
  `run_oodac_run(fs, sys, rargs)` is `pub`. `cmd_pm_launch.oo` already imports it.
  The file already calls `sq` from that import.
  DE1 can build a list with the CAS path and call `run_oodac_run`.
  No change to the gate string API is required. DE2 must not edit `cli/pm_launch.oo`.
  `run_oodac_run` already refuses a missing path, `--engine bc`, and `--fuzz`.
  It then calls `run_oodac` with `run` and the path. That is the same path as `ooda run`.
  `run_oodac` quotes tokens and starts `oodac` with `sh -c`. It does not wrap the payload.
  `run_oodac` then calls `process_exit(0)` or `process_exit(1)`.
  After `--exec`, the CLI will not print JSON and will not print `ooda launch: ok`.
  That is honest. Do not claim ok before the run finishes.
  Do not edit `host_run.oo` to return a Result. The plan forbids a silent shared edit.

